# DTF tier manifest: health-monitor-dependencies  (artifact-keeper#5651, 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: storage.s3 (MinIO) + scanners.mock-adapter (a python stand-in
# for the scanner adapter that answers GET /probe/healthy; TRIVY_ADAPTER_URL
# points at it).
#
# THE BUG (#5651)
# The health monitor (health log + alert state under
# /api/v1/admin/monitoring) checked the database, the Trivy server,
# OpenSearch, OpenSCAP and Dependency-Track only. A MinIO outage, an evicted
# scanner adapter and a Postgres restart between two 60 s checks all left
# only healthy rows. /readyz with the database down answered after 7-10 s:
# two sequential pool acquires before the dependency probes.
#
# THE FIX
# The monitor checks storage (through the /health storage check) and the
# scanner adapter (/probe/healthy), probes concurrently, and records a
# Postgres restart (pg_postmaster_start_time() after the last database check)
# as an `unavailable` row. /readyz runs one database query bounded to 1 s,
# alongside the dependency probes.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1). POST /admin/monitoring/check runs a
# check at once, so nothing waits for the 60 s scheduler.
#   (CONTROL)    with everything up, a check reports database healthy.
#   (FIX)        storage and scanner-adapter are checked and healthy.
#   (FIX)        MinIO stopped: storage is recorded unhealthy in the check, the
#                health log and the alert state, and
#                ak_health_monitor_up{service="storage"} is 0; MinIO started:
#                healthy again, the log has the unhealthy -> healthy row. RED
#                on main (no storage entry, no gauge).
#   (FIX)        mock adapter stopped: scanner-adapter recorded unavailable;
#                started: healthy. RED on main.
#   (FIX)        Postgres restarted between two checks: the health log has
#                exactly one database `unavailable` row "Postgres restarted at
#                ..." after two checks, and
#                ak_health_monitor_postgres_restarts_total >= 1. RED on main
#                (only healthy rows).
#   (FIX)        Postgres paused (hung, not refusing): /readyz answers 503
#                within 2.5 s. RED on main (its queries wait on the hung
#                connection).
#   (CONTROL)    with MinIO and the adapter both down, one check returns
#                within 8 s (the probes are bounded and concurrent); /readyz
#                is 200 again after Postgres is resumed.
COVERS="5651"
PROFILES="storage.s3 scanners.mock-adapter"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
